query_L0:
[Bug]: `browserContext.setStorageState()` never settles when the state contains IndexedDB and a page of the context is open on that origin

### Version

1.62.1

### Steps to reproduce


`browserContext.storageState({ indexedDB: true })` leaves an open IndexedDB connection in the page it reads from. That connection then blocks any later attempt to delete or recreate the database on that origin — including the one `browserContext.setStorageState()` performs internally. The result is a promise that never settles and never times out.

Two independent symptoms follow from the same leaked connection:

1. After `storageState({ indexedDB: true })`, `indexedDB.deleteDatabase()` in the page fires `onblocked` instead of `onsuccess`.
2. `setStorageState()` with a state containing IndexedDB hangs forever while a page of the context is open on that origin. It is not affected by `context.setDefaultTimeout()`.

Reproduction (Chromium, macOS; any origin works — the snippet uses `example.com`):

```js
const { chromium } = require('playwright');

const SEED = async () => {
  const req = indexedDB.open('rfdb', 1);
  req.onupgradeneeded = () => req.result.createObjectStore('kv');
  const db = await new Promise((res, rej) => {
    req.onsuccess = () => res(req.result);
    req.onerror = () => rej(req.error);
  });
  await new Promise((res, rej) => {
    const tx = db.transaction('kv', 'readwrite');
    tx.objectStore('kv').put('token-abc', 'auth');
    tx.oncomplete = () => res();
    tx.onerror = () => rej(tx.error);
  });
  db.close();
};

const DELETE = async () => {
  await new Promise((res, rej) => {
    const req = indexedDB.deleteDatabase('rfdb');
    req.onsuccess = () => res();
    req.onerror = () => rej(req.error);
    req.onblocked = () => rej(new Error('blocked'));
  });
};

(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();

  // Symptom 1: storageState({indexedDB}) leaves a connection open.
  for (const withSave of [false, true]) {
    const context = await browser.newContext();
    const page = await context.newPage();
    await page.goto('https://example.com/');
    await page.evaluate(SEED);
    if (withSave) await context.storageState({ indexedDB: true });
    let result = 'ok';
    try {
      await page.evaluate(DELETE);
    } catch {
      result = 'BLOCKED';
    }
    console.log(`storageState({indexedDB}) called first = ${withSave} -> deleteDatabase ${result}`);
    await context.close();
  }

  // Symptom 2: setStorageState() never settles, and ignores the context timeout.
  const context = await browser.newContext();
  context.setDefaultTimeout(3000);
  const page = await context.newPage();
  await page.goto('https://example.com/');
  await page.evaluate(SEED);
  const state = await context.storageState({ indexedDB: true });
  const outcome = await Promise.race([
    context.setStorageState(state).then(() => 'resolved', (e) => 'rejected: ' + e.message),
    new Promise((res) => setTimeout(() => res('still pending after 20s'), 20000)),
  ]);
  console.log(`setStorageState -> ${outcome}`);
  process.exit(0);
})();
```

### Expected behavior

`storageState({ indexedDB: true })` closes the IndexedDB connections it opens, so that the page it read from is left exactly as it was found. `setStorageState()` restores the state regardless of whether pages of the context are open on the affected origin, and — if it genuinely cannot proceed — rejects within the context timeout rather than hanging.

### Actual behavior


```
storageState({indexedDB}) called first = false -> deleteDatabase ok
storageState({indexedDB}) called first = true  -> deleteDatabase BLOCKED
setStorageState -> still pending after 20s
```

The promise returned by `setStorageState()` never settles. `context.setDefaultTimeout(3000)` has no effect on it.


### Additional context

### Workarounds

Anything that drops the page's IndexedDB connections before `setStorageState()` makes it resolve, and the data is then restored correctly:

| Between `storageState()` and `setStorageState()` | Result |
| --- | --- |
| nothing | hangs |
| `page.reload()` | resolves, value restored |
| `page.goto('about:blank')` | resolves, value restored |
| `page.close()` | resolves, value restored |
| restore into a different, freshly created context | resolves, value restored |

### Environment

- Playwright: 1.62.1
- Browser: Chromium (bundled)
- OS: macOS 15 (Darwin 25.5.0), arm64
- Node.js: v22.20.0

### Environment

```shell
System:
    OS: macOS 26.5.1
    CPU: (12) arm64 Apple M2 Max
    Memory: 71.11 MB / 32.00 GB
  Binaries:
    Node: 22.20.0 - /Users/XXX/.nvm/versions/node/v22.20.0/bin/node
    Yarn: 1.22.22 - /Users/XXX/.nvm/versions/node/v22.20.0/bin/yarn
    npm: 11.6.2 - /Users/XXX/.nvm/versions/node/v22.20.0/bin/npm
    pnpm: 10.30.3 - /Users/XXX/.nvm/versions/node/v22.20.0/bin/pnpm
  IDEs:
    VSCode: 1.132.0 - /usr/local/bin/code
    Claude Code: 2.1.233 - /Users/XXX/.local/bin/claude
    Codex: 0.147.0 - /Users/XXX/.local/bin/codex
  Languages:
    Bash: 3.2.57 - /bin/bash
  npmPackages:
    playwright: ^1.62.1 => 1.62.1
